---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AboutIntro from '../components/AboutIntro.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Brandon Greene',
  url: Astro.site?.href,
  description: 'High school student working on AI, mathematics and hardware.',
};
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Brandon Greene: tennis, school, the things he builds, the mountains and the water, and self-improvement at the centre of it."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <AboutIntro />

  <div class="wrap sheet">
    <div class="rail">
      <dl>
        <dt>Class of</dt>
        <dd>2029</dd>
        <dt>Right now</dt>
        <dd>Tennis and school</dd>
        <dt>Also</dt>
        <dd>Building things, the mountains and the water, piano</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="column" data-about-text>
      <!-- DRAFT: Brandon, every sentence below is built from what you told me
           (about-animation/interview.md in claude-learning). Rewrite anything
           in your own words; fill the marked gaps. The sections run in the
           same order as the ring above. -->

      <p class="lede" style="font-size:var(--step-1);line-height:1.5">
        I'm a high school sophomore, class of 2029. Right now school and tennis are the big two.
        Around them: the things I build, the mountains and the water, and a lot of thinking.
      </p>

      <h2 id="self-improvement">Self-improvement</h2>
      <p>
        I'm very big on self-improvement, and my values circle around it. <em>[To fill in: what that
        looks like for you, in your own words. A short video of you talking about it can go here.]</em>
      </p>

      <h2 id="tennis">Tennis</h2>
      <p>
        Tennis is a big part of me. I train with a private coach for at least twelve hours a week,
        play tournaments twice a month, and play on my high school team. I want to play in college.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's also where the <a href="/projects/foot-scanner">foot scanner</a> started: I play tennis
        and I have flat feet.
      </p>

      <h2 id="school">School</h2>
      <p>
        School is the other half of my week, and I take a rigorous course load. <em>[To fill in: the
        courses, and your GPA if you want it here.]</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also a few weeks into a year-long independent study in AI and machine learning, supervised
        by my computer science teacher. The idea came out of a conversation with my college advisor
        and lined up with things I already wanted to build.
      </p>

      <h2 id="projects">Projects</h2>
      <p>
        The main project is a foot scanner for custom orthotics: a phone-based scanning pipeline. It's
        in progress, not finished. The <a href="/log">build log</a> is where the week-to-week work
        lives, including the parts that don't work yet. Around it I work on machine learning and
        mathematics, and I 3D print. Everything is on the <a href="/projects">projects page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="coding">Coding</h2>
      <p>
        I've spent at least three years learning to program: HTML, CSS and JavaScript for the web,
        plus C++ and Python.
      </p>

      <h2 id="hobbies">Hobbies</h2>
      <p>
        Skiing is my favourite thing to do. I love biking, hiking in the mountains and the hills, and
        the water: I surf. I box and train three days a week.
      </p>
      <p>
        I grew up playing piano and taking swim lessons, and I still play piano now and then. I played
        chess competitively until high school.
      </p>

      <h2 id="mind">Mind</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a very psychological person. I have deep conversations with my friends, and I spend time
        thinking about myself and everything I have going on in life.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <!-- TODO: replace with the alias address once the domain is registered.
             Brandon's personal email must never appear here in plain text. -->
        <em>[Contact method not set up yet — an alias address on the site's own domain, once the
        domain is registered.]</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  // Phones: the sections fold behind their headings. The opening's pieces
  // link to #tennis, #hobbies and the rest, which open the matching section.
  import { collapseOnPhone, sectionsFrom } from '../scripts/phone-collapse';
  const text = document.querySelector('[data-about-text]');
  if (text) collapseOnPhone(sectionsFrom(text, 'h2'));
</script>

<style>
  /* Phones: the facts rail repeats what the opening's ring already says. */
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .rail { display: none; }
  }
</style>
